WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.300
Congrats on everything.
-Thank you.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.501
-I want to talk to you
about everything because

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:06.868
I want to know
what it even feels like.

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:08.567
You're in these giant movies.
-Yeah.

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:10.267
-The biggest movies.
I mean, between

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:13.801
Marvel's cinematic universe
and "Avatar"...

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:16.734
I mean, "Avatar's"
the biggest movie ever made.

00:00:16.734 --> 00:00:18.501
-Yes. Yes.
-Yeah.

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:21.367
And "Guardians of the Galaxy,"
I mean, what does it feel like

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.701
to be in the biggest --
-I'm pinching myself.

00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:26.000
-Yeah.
-It's not something that I

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.601
picked strategically.
-Yeah.

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:31.133
-I just -- I was just very lucky
to be picked, to be chosen.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:34.167
And I gave it 120%.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.934
The fact that these two movies
are the most successful ones,

00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:41.501
and I'm in them, it's not bad
for a girl from Queens.

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:43.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:45.734
-Not too shab--
it's not bad at all.

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.400
No, but you're so good.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.934
-Thank you.
-You're fantastic in it.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:51.033
You know,
I follow you on the socials.

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:53.434
You're fun.
And you -- you posted this.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:56.000
This is from
"Guardians of the Galaxy 3."

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.334
This is a bunch of you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:59.334
-Yeah.
-How many of you were there

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:00.734
with you -- with you?

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.400
-Like, four --
a minimum of four.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.968
It's a lot of me's.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:05.801
-And the thing is that,
these are created --

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:08.701
it's taken out of, like,
a cast of my head,

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.167
and it's so they can put
the wigs on

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:13.734
or any kind of additional
prosthetics that go on Gamora.

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:18.200
And -- and sometimes it's just
to put her in the background.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.601
Like -- kind of, like, maybe
like a "Where's Waldo?"

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:21.834
Like, "Where's Gamora?"
I don't know.

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:23.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:25.934
-So, like -- so, there's a
Gamora sometimes in the scene?

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:28.534
Are you in the scene, or just
sometimes there's just a Gamora?

00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:30.567
-Sometimes, like, let's say if
they're shooting a big

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:33.267
action sequence, and my
character is, like,

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:36.534
in the background
in certain parts of that set,

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:38.601
they'll just have -- like,
they'll just put a head, like,

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:41.167
running back and forth so the
computer can sort of track it.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.934
I don't know, guys.
It's high technology.

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:44.601
-Yeah, it's high tech--
Yeah.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:48.934
But I mean, "Guardians 3,"
this comes out next year, is it?

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:50.701
-Yes, next May.
-Next May.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:52.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.534
Just so fun.

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:57.000
And so it's really --
it's such a fun ride.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.334
-They're fun, you guys.
It is a fun ride.

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:02.701
I've -- I took my boys
to Disney earlier this year,

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:06.734
and my older sons are much more,
you know, precautious,

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:09.167
and they don't like to do, like,
roller coasters.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:11.300
My little one, his name is Zen.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.834
There's nothing Zen about Zen.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:15.667
Zen got on all the rides.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.467
He was only --
I mean, he's still 5.

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:18.968
-Aww.
-And then got on

00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:19.934
the Tower of Terror,
which is the

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:21.968
"Guardians of the Galaxy" ride.

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:23.767
And -- and I was like,
"How was it?"

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:24.968
He goes, "Oh, Mama.
I was so scared."

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:26.567
I'm like, "Did you see Mama?"
"I don't know.

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.067
No, I didn't see you."
-No, really?

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:29.367
-I'm like,
"Mama was in the ride."

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:31.167
He goes, "You were?"
-They have no idea.

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:33.033
-That might be one of the best
roller coasters I've ever

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:34.601
been on in --
-They don't think I'm cool

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.234
at all, so...
-Oh, my gosh!

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:38.667
But between that
and also the "Avatar" ride.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:39.834
-Yeah, I know.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:41.400
-Do they know
that you're that, as well?

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.501
-They do, they do.
But they -- they are --

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:44.868
My kids are softies.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:46.734
They don't like to watch things
that are too violent.

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:48.367
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah, not yet, not yet.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.334
We still have some time.
-Yeah, well, you have --

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:51.934
He's 5, and then the other boys?

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.934
-They just turned 8 yesterday.

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:55.434
-Ooh.
-Yeah.

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:57.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.334
There's a lot of Legos.
-Roblox?

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:02.501
-Yes, a lot of Roblox.
-I love Roblox.

00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:04.767
-But they don't really play
that much on the tablets.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:05.834
-Yeah?
-You know?

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:07.100
-Yeah.
-We do a lot of outdoor stuff.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.567
-My kids, either.
-Okay.

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:09.801
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, of course.

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:10.901
-But they do watch
a lot of Netflix.

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:12.000
-Yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.901
-Wah-wah.

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:15.367
-You know,
when I first saw "Avatar" --

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:17.801
I think a lot of people
would agree with me --

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:20.334
I'd never seen anything
like that in my lifetime.

00:03:20.334 --> 00:03:23.300
It was the coolest thing
I'd ever seen.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.901
I know James Cameron.
We're talking about

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.767
how cool this thing is gonna be
and different.

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:28.901
And I've seen 3-D movies.
When I was growing up,

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:31.534
a 3-D movie was something
somebody would be holding,

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:35.167
like, a pool stick, and they'd
be like, "Ah, ah, ah!"

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.968
And then you're like,
"Well, that's 3-D."

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:38.567
And then you see this,
and you go,

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:39.934
"Oh, this is
the most bizarre thing.

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:41.701
I feel like I'm in this world."
-Yeah.

00:03:41.701 --> 00:03:45.300
Well, I just -- if I seem a
little off and awfully quiet --

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:48.367
I know I'm very talkative --
it's because I just came back

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:51.234
from the screening.
I went to see "Avatar" today.

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:54.467
I'm still processing.
It's very emotional.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.634
I'm surprised my eyelashes
stayed on, you guys.

00:03:56.634 --> 00:03:58.167
I was, like --
I was, like, sobbing.

00:03:58.167 --> 00:03:59.334
-Good for you!
Come on.

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:00.701
-It's really special.
It's really --

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:02.834
it's really special.
And I can give you, like,

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:04.200
a little hint.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.634
It's about water.

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:07.501
[ Laughter ]
-Wow! Oh, my gosh.

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:08.901
[ Applause ]

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:10.901
Wow! We always get the scoop --
-A lot of water.

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:12.834
-We always get the scoop here
on "The Tonight Show," guys.

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:14.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:18.000
When "Avatar" was first pitched
to you, what did they pitch?

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.434
'Cause it's such
a brand-new world

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:20.968
and new characters
and new everything.

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:22.167
-You sound so nice.

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:23.601
Like, it was never
pitched to me.

00:04:23.601 --> 00:04:25.934
I was pitched for it.
Like, and then --

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:27.667
-Oh, really?
-Oh, my God, of course.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:30.167
If I could be so lucky to have
somebody like, "Yeah, pitch me.

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:31.601
What's this movie, Jim, about?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.267
-Yeah.
-Oh, my God.

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:35.200
-But what did you think it was?
Or what did you --

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.100
Describe it to me.
-I thought --

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.200
First, they told me that it was,
like, about this robot --

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.534
this female robot.

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:43.000
I thought it was like
"Alita: Battle Angel."

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.868
But it's set, like,
in the jungle.

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:47.501
And I was like, "Well, that
doesn't really make any sense.

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:50.033
Like, a warrior princess
was a robot, like a sentient --"

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:51.767
Like, "What is that?"
-Yeah.

00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:56.033
-But Mali Finn, who was the
casting director at that time,

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:58.234
who was later then --
you know, Margery Simkin took --

00:04:58.234 --> 00:04:59.901
took the part of casting it,

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:02.400
they would sometimes
just come in and call me.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.901
And I was still living
in New York at the time,

00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:05.133
and they would put me on tape.

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:07.434
And sometimes it was like,
"Bring some tight stuff.

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:09.667
I want you to climb
and do some cartwheels."

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:11.467
And I'm like, "Okay."
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:13.834
-So, I would come in, it's like,
"Well, we'll just play,"

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:15.300
and they would move
all the furniture.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.567
-Well, you have a dance
background, right?

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:18.834
-Yeah, yeah.
I feel like I was able

00:05:18.834 --> 00:05:21.934
to book the part
because of that.

00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:24.033
And then, one time,
they called me in,

00:05:24.033 --> 00:05:26.167
and I put myself
on tape again for them,

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:27.701
and they were like,
"Just make all these sounds."

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:29.234
I'm like, "What kind of sounds?"

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:30.367
[ Tongue rolling sound ]

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:32.534
[ Laughter ]
And I'm like, "Well, okay."

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:34.701
-You're like, "What is this
movie remotely?"

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.634
-And I'm thinking like, "Okay.
James Cameron,

00:05:36.634 --> 00:05:39.968
a robot warrior princess
that's in a jungle,

00:05:39.968 --> 00:05:42.601
and I'm doing R, like --
rolling my R's."

00:05:42.601 --> 00:05:44.367
I'm like, "I don't know
what this is, but I dig it.

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:45.701
I dig it."
-Yeah.

00:05:45.701 --> 00:05:48.234
Yeah, and then so, you do
all that, and you go, "Okay."

00:05:48.234 --> 00:05:50.534
And did -- when did you finally
get to meet James Cameron?

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:54.300
-They flew me from New York
to Los Angeles

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:56.100
and drove me to Lightstorm.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.534
-Now, do you feel good
at this point?

00:05:57.534 --> 00:05:59.100
Or are you like,
"I'm in the running"?

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.267
-I mean -- yeah, I'm excited.

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:03.834
But I was always, like,
a very happy-go-lucky,

00:06:03.834 --> 00:06:05.400
like, a happy girl from Queens,
I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.567
I'm gonna go meet my idol,
like, James Cameron."

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:09.801
-Yeah.
-And they lock me in an office,

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:12.400
which was a bit scary.
-Yeah.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:13.934
-And they gave me the script.

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:15.300
And the script was, like,
this thick.

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:17.133
-Oh, so this is very private.

00:06:17.133 --> 00:06:18.200
They don't let anyone
look at this.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:19.167
-No, no.
-That's why you're in this

00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:20.334
private office.
Oh, I understand.

00:06:20.334 --> 00:06:21.934
-And they gave me
three hours to read it.

00:06:21.934 --> 00:06:24.000
I took six.
Because it was just

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.067
all the directions
describing the whole world

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:29.367
of Pandora was just
really bizarre to me and I --

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:31.334
English is not
my first language,

00:06:31.334 --> 00:06:32.934
so that was a little hard.

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:36.334
And then Jim walks in,
and he was so nice.

00:06:36.334 --> 00:06:38.467
And then he says, "Are you ready
to meet yourself?"

00:06:38.467 --> 00:06:40.133
And I was like, "What?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:43.534
And at that moment, my soul,
like, left my body.

00:06:43.534 --> 00:06:45.033
-"So, are you ready
to meet yourself?"

00:06:45.033 --> 00:06:46.567
-Yeah, that's what he told me.

00:06:46.567 --> 00:06:48.467
And then he walks me
to his office.

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:51.167
I see this big wheel of a ship,

00:06:51.167 --> 00:06:53.601
and I had no idea
it was the "Titanic" wheel.

00:06:53.601 --> 00:06:56.100
I see the arm of
the Terminator.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.501
-Oh, my God.
-I just -- I was just like,

00:06:57.501 --> 00:06:58.767
"Oh, my God.
This is --

00:06:58.767 --> 00:07:00.501
I'm having
an out-of-body experience."

00:07:00.501 --> 00:07:03.300
-Exactly, that's his office.
-And his office was beautiful

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:05.934
and big and just, like,
all these, like, you know,

00:07:05.934 --> 00:07:08.567
things that he had kept
from all of his films.

00:07:08.567 --> 00:07:11.133
And then, on a coffee table
was a sculpture

00:07:11.133 --> 00:07:12.901
of my character, Neytiri.

00:07:12.901 --> 00:07:15.267
And as I'm observing
the sculpture,

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:18.200
he's sitting across from me,
like, observing me.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.934
And I thought in my mind, like,
"That's not weird.

00:07:19.934 --> 00:07:21.200
That's not weird."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.234
-"Don't act weird."
-"It's all -- it's all going

00:07:23.234 --> 00:07:24.868
in the movie somehow.
It's all going in."

00:07:24.868 --> 00:07:26.334
When did you find out
that you got the part?

00:07:26.334 --> 00:07:28.334
-Like -- like, maybe
like a week or two later.

00:07:28.334 --> 00:07:29.434
-Do you remember where you were?

00:07:29.434 --> 00:07:32.067
-Yes, I was in my apartment
in Queens.

00:07:32.067 --> 00:07:35.634
-Uh-huh.
-Changing my nephew's diaper.

00:07:35.634 --> 00:07:36.834
[ Laughter ]
-Really?

00:07:36.834 --> 00:07:39.601
-Yeah. I had --
I had nanny duties that day.

00:07:39.601 --> 00:07:40.901
And my mother walks in,
and she go--

00:07:40.901 --> 00:07:44.033
with her -- with my cellphone,
"Zoe, Zoe, it's --

00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:47.801
They say it's James Cameron."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.801 --> 00:07:49.934
And I'm like, "Oh, my God!
Okay, hold the baby wipes.

00:07:49.934 --> 00:07:51.100
Oh, my God!"
-"Hold the diaper!

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:52.534
Hold the phone!
Hold the diaper!"

00:07:52.534 --> 00:07:54.400
Yeah, you pick up the diaper,
"Hello?" Yeah.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:56.734
-My sister, my mom, and, like,
my little nephew's, like,

00:07:56.734 --> 00:07:59.934
popping up his face.
And I'm like, "Hello?"

00:07:59.934 --> 00:08:02.367
And he's like,
"Hey, Zoe, it's Jim.

00:08:02.367 --> 00:08:04.067
I just wanted to invite you
to join us,

00:08:04.067 --> 00:08:05.934
and I want you to play Neytiri."

00:08:05.934 --> 00:08:08.000
And I still get teary-eyed
because it was --

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.701
it was definitely, like,
a very big opportunity

00:08:09.701 --> 00:08:11.467
and a very big
dream come true for me.

00:08:11.467 --> 00:08:13.968
And then, I didn't need to cry
'cause my mom and my sister

00:08:13.968 --> 00:08:16.567
and my nephew were sobbing.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.567 --> 00:08:19.200
I'm like, "Oh, my God!"
-We're so happy for you.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.467
Aw, you're awesome.

